<section class="section narrow"><p class="eyebrow">WHY OPEN INNOVATION</p><h1>TouchGrass AI is intentionally local.</h1><p>The project treats open AI as infrastructure, not decoration. The web application is PHP 8.5, data is SQLite, and the AI boundary points to an Ollama-compatible local runtime. That means the same application can swap models without rewriting the outdoor workflow.</p><div class="cards"><article class="mini-card"><h3>Private by default</h3><p>Field notes and preferences remain in your own Docker volume unless you explicitly export them.</p></article><article class="mini-card"><h3>Model freedom</h3><p>Change <code>OLLAMA_MODEL</code> and keep the PHP application unchanged.</p></article><article class="mini-card"><h3>Offline after setup</h3><p>The PWA shell works offline; local AI works without internet once the selected model is downloaded.</p></article><article class="mini-card"><h3>Screen-short UX</h3><p>The output is an activity plan with a deliberate “phone-away challenge,” not an endless chat interface.</p></article></div><h2>Safety boundary</h2><p>AI suggestions are not live navigation, emergency advice, weather forecasting, or guaranteed wildlife identification. Check official local conditions before leaving and use ordinary outdoor safety judgment.</p><p><a class="button" href="/">Back to field mode</a></p></section>
